<title>FRANCE: French March consumer prices up unrevised 0.1 pct.</title>
<headline>French March consumer prices up unrevised 0.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE gave the following data:</p>
<p>				    Mar	  Feb	Mar 1996</p>
<p> Month-on-month inflation   0.1	  0.2	  0.6</p>
<p> Year-on-year inflation     1.1	  1.6	  2.3</p>
<p> CPI Index (base 1990)    115.0	114.9	113.8</p>
<p>INSEE gave the following breakdown of the consumer price index for all households in mainland France, base 1990.</p>
<p>     Category		  Weight(pct) index  1-mo   3-mo  yr/yr</p>
<p> Food excluding tobacco	 20.20    107.8  -0.4    0.4    0.2</p>
<p> Private-sector manufactures  32.77    109.0   0.6    0.4    0.0</p>
<p> Private-sector services	19.64    126.0   0.1    0.6    1.6</p>
<p> Energy				8.66    114.9  -0.7    0.0    3.9</p>
<p> Public services ex energy     6.46    130.6   0.5    2.3    2.8</p>
<p> Rent, water			 6.68    130.4   0.2    0.6    1.9</p>
<p> Health spending		   5.59    110.0   0.0   -0.2    0.5</p>
<p> Total excluding tobacco	98.02    113.9   0.1    0.4    0.9</p>
<p>					 Mar   Last 3 months    yr/yr</p>
<p> EU harmonised inflation:	0.1	  0.6	   1.1</p>
<p> EU harmonised infl. index     Mar	  Feb	   Mar 96</p>
<p>					 101.1	101.0	 100.0</p>
<p>NOTE - European Union harmonised data complies with definitions in the Maastricht treaty and is meant to allow comparisons between member states. Harmonised inflation data was issued for the first time in March, data for the month of January.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
